<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-4102] JSONObject.getJSONObject() may cause program crash if element does not exist.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-4102</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Location:&#160;elasticsearch/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/elasticsearch/client/HttpBasedClient.java:77&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to the description at&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wink.apache.org/documentation/1.2.1/api/org/apache/wink/json4j/JSONObject.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://wink.apache.org/documentation/1.2.1/api/org/apache/wink/json4j/JSONObject.html&lt;/a&gt;, the method &quot;getJSONObject(String)&quot; may throw &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wink.apache.org/documentation/1.2.1/api/org/apache/wink/json4j/JSONException.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;JSONException&lt;/a&gt;&quot;, which may risk the program in crashing. However, the method &quot;optJSONObject(String)&quot; will return a default value (null) if&#160;the element does not exist. To ensure safety, the latter should be preferred.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
